# PRD & FLOW Enforcement Rules

All implementations MUST strictly follow:
- PRD.md (Phase 1 scope first)
- FLOW.md (defined user & data flow)

## 1. Page Flow (Non-negotiable)

Allowed navigation order:
Login (/)  
→ Post List (/posts)  
→ Post Create (/posts/new)  
→ Post Detail (/posts/:id)  
→ Back to List

Forbidden:
- Skipping steps
- Multi-branch flows
- AI result shown outside Post Detail page

## 2. Study Post Lifecycle

A Study Post MUST:
1. Be created BEFORE AI processing
2. Exist independently of AI results
3. Store AI results only AFTER AI processing completes

AI result MUST NEVER:
- Exist without a StudyPost
- Be generated on list page
- Be recalculated automatically on view

## 3. Phase Boundary Rules

Phase 1:
- In-memory Context state ONLY
- Mock AI, Mock OCR/STT allowed
- No real Supabase persistence

Phase 2:
- Mentioned ONLY as future hints (comments / TODO)
- NEVER partially implemented

If a feature belongs to Phase 2:
→ show UX hint or placeholder
→ do NOT implement logic
